    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0334" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13479: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-26T12:00:00+02:00">July 26,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. Bucharest’s 696, July 25th.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d345-f1"/> Bulgaria is
                    completely tranquil with Government forces in absolute control. I spoke to the
                    King here yesterday. Prime Minister and Foreign Minister are on way back <pb
                        facs="0335" n="323" xml:id="pg323"/> from Rome and all other important
                    members of his Government are in Sofia.</p>
                <p>Pro-Russian sentiment has to some extent been neutralized by Germany’s gift of
                    new territories to Bulgaria.</p>
                <p>Only in the event of severe German reverses in Russia could there be a
                    probability of a serious Communist uprising.</p>
                <p>The use of Bulgarian air fields by the Russians is out of the question. The
                    presence of Rumanian troops in Bulgaria is also almost certainly untrue. It
                    would be fiercely resented by the Bulgarians who despise and detest the Rumanian
                    people, officials and soldiers.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Bucharest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
